WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.115 --> 00:00:02.284
(water dripping)

00:00:02.284 --> 00:00:04.600
(slow music)

00:00:04.600 --> 00:00:08.767
- To play the instrument that
is utilizing our gentle Earth,

00:00:11.829 --> 00:00:15.501
it's like you're becoming
one with the instrument

00:00:15.501 --> 00:00:17.084
in a very true way.

00:00:17.944 --> 00:00:20.027
You just sit and go, yes.

00:00:26.769 --> 00:00:29.825
We're looking at The
Great Stalacpipe Organ

00:00:29.825 --> 00:00:33.691
of the Luray Caverns in Luray, Virginia.

00:00:33.691 --> 00:00:37.518
When I press a key, it
sends an electrical pulse

00:00:37.518 --> 00:00:42.231
up to a rubber-tipped mallet,
which strikes the stalactite,

00:00:42.231 --> 00:00:46.401
causing it to vibrate, and
producing a incredibly beautiful

00:00:46.401 --> 00:00:47.484
musical tone.

00:00:48.743 --> 00:00:52.076
The area that the
strikers cover is roughly

00:00:52.076 --> 00:00:56.234
three and a half acres,
which then makes it literally

00:00:56.234 --> 00:00:59.656
the world's largest musical instrument.

00:00:59.656 --> 00:01:02.062
(water dripping)

00:01:02.062 --> 00:01:05.479
It is a very gentle sound, very peaceful.

00:01:06.935 --> 00:01:09.774
There's only one like it in the world,

00:01:09.774 --> 00:01:13.297
and it's something incredibly different

00:01:13.297 --> 00:01:15.464
and wonderfully beautiful.

00:01:17.009 --> 00:01:19.759
(water dripping)

